{
  "plugin": "lacrosse-scoreboard",
  "_comment": "Lacrosse keeps one manager per league and mode as a plain attribute -- ncaa_mens_live, ncaa_womens_recent and so on -- rather than in a dict, and only builds them when that league's enabled flag is set, so the config below turns both leagues on. Every mode's display() returns early unless games_list is populated, and the live path also reads live_games and active_celebration. display_mode picks which of the six screens is drawn. The card reads home_logo_path/away_logo_path off the game dict as Path objects. Teams, scores and records are invented; the crests bundled in the core are grey placeholders, so they render as blocks.",
  "defaults": {
    "width": 128,
    "height": 32,
    "scale": 6,
    "freeze_time": "2026-04-18T17:00:00+00:00",
